 36CA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2022La10:                          
 36CA2c  Phys Rev Lett 129, 122501 (2022); and the Supplemental Material.       
 36CA c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), Sept 16, 2022.                        
 36CA c  2022La10: {+36}Ca and {+37}Ca secondary beams incident on CRYPTA       
 36CA2c  hydrogen target obtained from {+9}Be({+40}Ca,X),E=95 MeV/nucleon       
 36CA3c  primary reaction, followed by separation of fragments using LISE3      
 36CA4c  spectrometer at GANIL facility. Measured outgoing {+36}Ca ions, E(d),  
 36CA5c  I(d), E(t), I(t),  angles of deuterons and tritons,                    
 36CA6c  ({+36}Ca)({+37}Ca)-coin, ({+36}Ca)({+38}Ca)-coin, ({+36}Ca)d-coin,     
 36CA7c  ({+36}Ca)t-coin, ({+36}Ca)p-coin, ({+36}Ca)2p-coin, using zero-degree  
 36CA8c  detection (ZDD) system for {+36}Ca, multiwire detectors CATS array for 
 36CA9c  {+37}Ca, six MUST2 telescopes with double-sided Silicon strip detector 
 36CAAc  (DSSSD) and 16 CsI crystals for deuterons, tritons and protons. Deduced
 36CABc  levels, proton resonances, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors,  
 36CACc  configurations and their amplitudes, mirror energy differences (MEDs)  
 36CADc  of levels in {+36}Ca and {+36}S. DWBA analysis. Comparison with        
 36CAEc  shell-model calculations with configuration interaction (Sm CI) using  
 36CAFc  the sd-pf valence space, and with spectroscopic data for mirror nucleus
 36CAGc  {+36}S.                                                                
 36CA c  {+1}H({+37}Ca,d) reaction analyzed as {+37}Ca(p,d); and                
 36CA2c  {+1}H({+38}Ca,t) reaction as {+38}Ca(p,t).                             
